    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI wanted to have the first item be autoselected, so I set `vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,popup,noinsert'`, but this setting causes a small visual glitch: if the first item has no info, but when typing a letter the next one has info, two menus will overlap, one non decorated\n\nFor instance:\nI am using friendly snippets and lua_ls lsp:\nI type f:\n\n<img width=\"357\" height=\"99\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e1189eb-cfa1-4a9d-aede-543988706e0f\" />\n\nthe no info message shows\nI type o:\n\n<img width=\"533\" height=\"93\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d54dfb7b-7a08-408c-a7fb-0bf4c47bfefe\" />\n\nThe two menus overlap\n\nTyping r doesn't solve close the menu, and with fuzzy matching enabled typing p selects the second option but and updates both popup menus, without closing the faulty one\n\nFor the record, this is what the menu should look like:\n\n<img width=\"533\" height=\"93\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b82e80e1-51ad-4aa4-b21a-db1c6a21fb59\" />\n\n(displayed like that when the first entry when typing has info)\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. set `vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,popup,noinsert'`\n1. Ensure you have a entry that will display first with no info, and one that will display next with info\n1. Type the first common letter of the two entries, it should display no info\n1. Type the second letter of the entry with a description to get the overlapped menu ",
