            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> I wanted to have the first item be autoselected, so I set vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,popup,noinsert', but this setting causes a small visual glitch: if the first item has no info, but when typing a letter the next one has info, two menus will overlap, one non decorated\n\nThis is a direct result of `popup` flag. Here is a part of `:h 'completeopt'`:\n\n> Show extra information about the currently selected completion in a popup window.\n\nRemoving the `popup` flag should not show the second (borderless) window on top.",
